-- title:
--   Stalks to packages for the q=3 supersingular level model
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and the level is rigidified by a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Further standing data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$); a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$ over $\kappa:=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, where $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$ is the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`, the hypothesis `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly the set $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,\kappa$ of places $w$ that are rational (i.e. $\kappa$ surjects onto the residue field of $w$), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w$-value of the generator `jGeomGen` in the set `ssJSet q`; a distinguished element $s\in W$; the inclusion `hle` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field) in $\bar F:=\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, with $H=\ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; and a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$ — a valuation subring of the source together with a surjective residue homomorphism whose kernel is its maximal ideal, compatible with $A\to\kappa$, with the rescaling property and a degree- and order-preserving map on places — subject to `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   The small-constant layer consists of: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field, together with `hκ`: every $a\in A$ differs from some $c\in k_0\cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. In addition a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$ is fixed, together with $\zeta_0\in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally the layers: an index type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K_n$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ finite over $k_0$, and valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ with $x\in A_n$ if and only if $x\in A$, so $A_n=A\cap K_n$.
--
--   The field $\bar F$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\bar F$. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq\bar F$ whose compositum with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $\bar F$; for every field $F_{ss}$ with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\bar F$ to $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F$ meeting the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ exactly in $A$, with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $F_{ss}$ with kernel its maximal ideal, compatible with $A\to\kappa$, and such that every nonzero element of $\bar F$ has a constant multiple with nonzero residue); and for every finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$, every family of subrings $S(Q,n)\subseteq\bar F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi(Q,n):A_n[X]\to S(Q,n)$ and $\chi(Q,n):S(Q,n)\to\kappa$, and sets $D(Q,n)$ of places of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (all indexed by places $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ and by $n\in\iota$), the stalk hypothesis below implies the package conclusion below. Here a place of $F$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $K$, distinct from $F$ and a principal ideal ring; $P.\mathrm{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of its adic valuation, $P$ is rational when $K$ surjects onto its residue field, and $P.\mathrm{evalAt} f$ is the preimage in $K$ of the residue of $f$ (and $0$ if $f$ is not in the valuation ring). Write $F_n$ for the compositum, inside $\bar F$, of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_n$ with $F_0$.
--
--   The stalk hypothesis is the conjunction of: (N1) $\#N=q+1$; (N2) layerwise data at each $Q\notin N$; (N3) compatibility in $n$; (N4) separation; (N5) cusp avoidance; (N6) level equivariance. In detail, (N2) asserts for every $Q\notin N$ and every $n\in\iota$: (i) the map $A_n\to\kappa$ sending $a$ to the residue of $a$ in $A$ is surjective; (ii) the image of $A_n$ in $\bar F$ lies in $S(Q,n)$; (iii) $\varphi(Q,n)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; (iv) $\varphi(Q,n)(C a)$ equals the image of $a$ in $\bar F$ for $a\in A_n$; (v) $\chi(Q,n)(\varphi(Q,n)(Ca))$ is the residue of $a$; (vi) $\chi(Q,n)(\varphi(Q,n)(X))=0$; (vii) for every $c\in A_n$ with vanishing residue in $\kappa$ there is exactly one ring homomorphism $\chi:S(Q,n)\to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi(Q,n)(Ca))=a$ for all $a\in A_n$, with residue of $\chi f$ equal to $\chi(Q,n)f$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi(Q,n)(X))=c$; (viii) every $f\in S(Q,n)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi(Q,n)f$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; (ix) $\varphi(Q,n)(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of its $R$-residue is $1$; (x) $D(Q,n)$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ such that every $f\in S(Q,n)$ lies in the valuation ring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt} f\in A$, and such that the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt} f$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi(Q,n)f=0$; (xi) $\varphi(Q,n)(X)\neq\varphi(Q,n)(Cc)$ for all $c\in A_n$; (xii) $S(Q,n)$ is local with maximal ideal the vanishing locus of $\chi(Q,n)$, Noetherian, and a unique factorisation domain; (xiii) $S(Q,n)\subseteq F_n$, and every element of $F_n$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in S(Q,n)$, $h\neq 0$; (xiv) linear disjointness: for $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K_n$ and $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to F_n$, $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$; (xv) for every ring homomorphism $\chi:S(Q,n)\to A_n$ splitting the constants and compatible with residues, $\ker\chi$ is generated by $\varphi(Q,n)(X)-\varphi(Q,n)(C(\chi(\varphi(Q,n)(X))))$; (xvi) there is a nonzero generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$ such that $\varphi(Q,n)(C\varpi)$ is prime, such that an element of $F_n$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it is $g/h$ with $g,h\in S(Q,n)$ and $\varphi(Q,n)(C\varpi)\nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S(Q,n)$ not associated to $\varphi(Q,n)(C\varpi)$ and every $x\in S(Q,n)$ some monic polynomial over $A_n$, transported by $\varphi(Q,n)\circ C$ and evaluated at $x$, is divisible by $p$; (xvii) there is a finite subset $G$ of $S(Q,n)$ such that every $f\in S(Q,n)$ satisfies $fh=g$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ a unit of $S(Q,n)$. Clause (N3) asserts the existence of a monotonicity witness $S(Q,n)\subseteq S(Q,n')$ whenever $K_n\subseteq K_{n'}$, together with: $S(Q,n')$ contained in the subring generated by $S(Q,n)$ and the image of $A_{n'}$ when $K_n\subseteq K_{n'}$; the coordinates $\varphi(Q,n)(X)$ independent of $n$ as elements of $\bar F$; and $\chi(Q,n')$ restricting to $\chi(Q,n)$ on $S(Q,n)$. Clause (N4): if $Q,Q'\notin N$ and some place $P$ lies in both $D(Q,n)$ and $D(Q',n)$ for some $n$, then $Q=Q'$. Clause (N5): for $Q\notin N$, every $n$ and every $P\in D(Q,n)$, $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image in $\bar F$ of the $q$-expansion $j_q$ of the $j$-function is $\ge 0$. Clause (N6): for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(\bar F)$ generated by the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ preserves $N$ in the strong sense that $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q\in N\iff Q\in N$ for every place $Q$, and for $Q\notin N$ and every $n$ the transported disc $\{P:\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D(Q,n)\}$ equals $D(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q,n)$.
--
--   The conclusion is again a conjunction of six clauses. First, $\#N=q+1$. Second, for every $Q\notin N$: for every $n\in\iota$ the clauses (i)–(x) above hold verbatim, followed by four further clauses and then (xvii) verbatim. The four further clauses are: (a) for every ring homomorphism $\chi:S(Q,n)\to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi(Q,n)(Ca))=a$ for all $a\in A_n$ and with residue of $\chi f$ equal to $\chi(Q,n)f$ for all $f$, there is exactly one place $P$ with $P\in D(Q,n)$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt} f$ equal to the image of $\chi f$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for every $f\in S(Q,n)$; (b) for every $P\in D(Q,n)$ and every $f\in F_n$, $f$ lies in the valuation ring of $P$ if and only if $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in S(Q,n)$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt} h\neq 0$; (c) every nonzero $f\in F_n$ with $P.\mathrm{ord} f=0$ for all $P\in D(Q,n)$ admits a nonzero $c\in K_n$ and a unit $u$ of $S(Q,n)$ with $c f=u$ in $\bar F$; (d) every $f\in F_n$ that lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation ring of every $P\in D(Q,n)$ lies in $S(Q,n)$. The second clause then ends with the compatibility statement (N3) for that $Q$, repeated verbatim. The remaining three conjuncts of the conclusion are the separation clause (N4), the cusp-avoidance clause (N5) and the level-equivariance clause (N6), each repeated verbatim.
--
--   Thus the conclusion retains the clauses (i)–(x) and (xvii) of the hypothesis together with (N3)–(N6), discards the structural clauses (xi)–(xvi), and adds the bijection between $A_n$-sections and points of the disc, the description of the local rings of points of the disc inside $F_n$, the unit principle on the disc, and the recognition of $S(Q,n)$ as the functions of $F_n$ that are $R$-integral and regular on the disc.
--
--   This is the step passing, at the supersingular points of the level-$q^2M'$ model with $q=3$ and the rigid-level guard $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$, $\ell_g\mid M'$, from the étale-stalk description of the local rings $S(Q,n)$ at a smooth point to the full geometric description of the associated residue discs: points of the disc correspond to $A_n$-valued sections, local rings are localisations of $S(Q,n)$, functions without zeros or poles on the disc are constants times units, and $R$-integral functions regular on the disc lie in $S(Q,n)$. It rests on [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint), whose hypothesis on principality of valuation subrings is supplied through [`ModularCurve.isCurveOver_and_essFiniteType_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isCurveOver_and_essFiniteType_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField), [`ModularCurve.JOneES.exists_transcendental_finiteDimensional_laurentBaseChange`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JOneES.exists_transcendental_finiteDimensional_laurentBaseChange) and [`ValuationSubring.isPrincipalIdealRing_of_finiteDimensional_adjoin`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.isPrincipalIdealRing_of_finiteDimensional_adjoin), and it feeds the construction of the supersingular prolongation and its covering by residue discs in the $q=3$ column.
